{
  "abstract": "A Lean formalization of Theorem 1.1 of A quasi-Riemann hypothesis for Dedekind zeta functions: for every number field K, its Dedekind zeta function has no zeros in Re(s) > 1 - 1/6000. The formal statement asserts the existence of a holomorphic function away from 1 that agrees with Mathlib's Dedekind zeta function for Re(s) > 1 and is nonzero for Re(s) > 5999/6000 with s different from 1. This repository contains the substantive Lean development, including its Challenge and Solution.",
